  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 10–15 days show a persistent rise (higher highs / higher lows), add a positive level shift to the whole path. In these samples the model is ~+5 to +15 EUR too low, with the gap widening with horizon.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: apply an increasing uplift with lead time (small at t+1–t+3, larger from ~t+7 onward). The model’s slope is too flat versus realized outcomes during rallies.",
    "Lag in regime change: after a breakout above the recent 30d range, treat it as a new regime rather than mean-reverting; increase the forecast drift for the next 2–4 weeks instead of pulling back toward the prior mean.",
    "Peak/plateau mis-timing: the model often predicts an early peak and then declines while the market continues to grind higher. Delay any projected reversal unless there is clear evidence of topping (e.g., multiple lower closes).",
    "Underestimated volatility in bull runs: widen the upper tail / allow larger daily gains during strong momentum periods; don’t cap moves near recent highs."
  ]
}
